        "code": {
          "text": "Reported oral HSV-1 prodrome and episode frequency"
        },
        "subject": {
          "reference": "Patient/patient-1"
        },
        "valueString": "Typical prodrome is tingling/burning of the right upper lip, followed by blisters and crusting. Today the patient reports mild tingling and feeling that an episode is about to start; no vesicles yet. Reports flares every month or two now, previously hardly ever; history is unreliable and dates are unclear."
      }
